  "id": "COMPOUND:22101 - PROTEIN:6319",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. This interaction is mediated through the interferon alpha/beta receptor (IFNAR), which is a target of both Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide and Ertugliflozin. The shared targeting of IFNAR by these compounds implies a common pathway in which the drug–target relationship is established through receptor activation. The presence of a consistent target in the pathway, IFNAR, supports the notion that Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide may influence UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a receptor-mediated mechanism. The evidence is further strengthened by the presence of a direct target relationship between Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide and IFNAR, which is a well-characterized receptor involved in immune and inflammatory responses. The integration of these pathways suggests that the drug may modulate UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a mechanism involving the interferon signaling cascade, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
